e":"en"},"830":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap-17","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap#planning-guidance-for-contributors","content":"Treat top-level directories as evidence of active work areas, not as guarantees of release timing.","locale":"en"},"831":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap-18","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap#planning-guidance-for-contributors","content":"Avoid repeating unpublished storage or protocol promises that are not backed by the reference repository state.","locale":"en"},"832":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap-19","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap#getting-involved","content":"Comment on relevant GitHub Issues if a task already exists.","locale":"en"},"833":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap-20","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap#getting-involved","content":"Use GitHub Discussions for broader proposals or roadmap suggestions.","locale":"en"},"834":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap-21","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Contribute/roadmap#getting-involved","content":"When sending doc updates, keep commands and feature descriptions tied to what the reference repo actually builds, ships, and tests.","locale":"en"},"835":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","type":"page","content":"Bare Metal Deployment","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deploy Curvine Cluster","Distributed Mode"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","locale":"en"},"836":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"Logical Deployment Architecture","locale":"en"},"837":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#startup-commands","content":"Startup Commands","locale":"en"},"838":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","content":"Before deployment, you need to create installation packages and modify configuration files.","locale":"en"},"839":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"The following diagram shows the logical architecture of a Curvine bare metal deployment. The **cluster core** consists only of Master and Worker processes; they must be started for the cluster to operate. FUSE is an **optional** access method and is **not** part of the cluster startup—you only need it when applications require a POSIX mount point.","locale":"en"},"840":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"**Cluster core (required):** Start `curvine-master` and `curvine-worker` on the intended hosts. The cluster is operational once Master and Workers are running; you can use the CLI (`cv`) or SDK without FUSE.","locale":"en"},"841":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"**FUSE (optional):** Start `curvine-fuse` only when you need a POSIX filesystem mount (e.g. for legacy tools or scripts). FUSE is not a core service—the cluster does not depend on it to start or run.","locale":"en"},"842":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"When Load and Export jobs need independent scheduling, deploy Transfer as a\nseparate optional service after the cluster is healthy. It does not join the\nMaster Raft group and does not require a Master or Worker configuration change.\nSee Deploy Transfer on Bare Metal.","locale":"en"},"843":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"**FUSE is not part of cluster startup.** The Curvine cluster is formed by Master and Worker nodes. FUSE is one of several access methods (along with CLI and SDK) and is only needed when applications require a local mount point.","locale":"en"},"844":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#logical-deployment-architecture","content":"Each worker needs to have its own determined IP. In multi-network interface environments, it is recommended to explicitly specify the IP through environment variables to avoid automatically reading unexpected network interface addresses.","locale":"en"},"845":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/Bare-Metal-Deployment#startup-commands","content":"Bare metal deployment requires manually starting the **cluster core** (master and worker). Optionally start FUSE on nodes where you need a POSIX mount:","locale":"en"},"846":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","type":"page","content":"Configuration Reference","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deploy Curvine Cluster","Distributed Mode"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","locale":"en"},"847":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#config-sources","content":"Config Sources","locale":"en"},"848":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#how-the-config-is-loaded","content":"How the config is loaded","locale":"en"},"849":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/