Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#journal","content":"Key points:","locale":"en"},"1021":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-174","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#journal","content":"`journal_addrs` must list the Raft peers, and the effective local hostname must match one of the entries (or `net_interface` must resolve to a matching IPv4). Otherwise startup fails.","locale":"en"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-175","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#journal","content":"`retain_checkpoint_num` also defines the retained log window (`retain_checkpoint_num × snapshot_entries` entries). Raising it increases journal disk usage.","locale":"en"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-176","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#journal","content":"`leader_create_snapshot` defaults to creating snapshots only for a single-node group. A multi-node group with this key unset has no leader-side log compaction and logs an error every few minutes; set `leader_create_snapshot = true` for production HA clusters.","locale":"en"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-177","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#journal","content":"`ignore_reply_error = true` can make a Master permanently diverge from its peers. Use it only for disaster recovery, never as a normal setting.","locale":"en"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-178","page_id":"/d