nuals/Access/fuse","content":"**FUSE is an optional access method.** The Curvine cluster (Master + Worker) must be running first. FUSE is only needed when applications require a POSIX mount point. See Deployment Architecture for the role of each component.","locale":"en"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Curvine cluster** is running (Master and Worker started). See Bare Metal Deployment or Quick Start.","locale":"en"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Configuration**: The node where FUSE runs must have access to the cluster config (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`) and correct Master address.","locale":"en"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Supported systems**: FUSE 2 and FUSE 3 are supported; behavior may vary by distribution. See Supported Linux Distributions.","locale":"en"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"Run from the installation directory (e.g. `build/dist` or the extracted release package):","locale":"en"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default mount path**: `/curvine-fuse`","locale":"en"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default config**: `conf/curvine-cluster.toml` (relative to current wor