ve\nworkers, preferring the structured `component_info.release_version` reported on\nheartbeat and falling back to the legacy `software_version` string:","locale":"en"},"2714":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-55","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"See Version Management and Compatibility for the\nmeaning of these versions and how the master evaluates mixed-version peers.","locale":"en"},"2715":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-56","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"The current implementation strips `hostname:port` down to `hostname` before calling the decommission API. The port is mainly for readability and consistent input format.","locale":"en"},"2716":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"**Usage:** `cv fs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]`","locale":"en"},"2717":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-58","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"`fs` adds one command-level global switch:","locale":"en"},"2718":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-59","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option         | Description                                                                             |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--cache-only` | Query / operate only on data already cached in Curvine, disabling the unified UFS view. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"2719":{"i