r `chmod` / `chown` is exposed as the third positional argument `[RECURSIVE]`, not as a `--recursive` flag. Permission strings support octal values such as `755` / `0o755` and symbolic forms such as `u=rwx,g=rx,o=rx`. `chown` supports `user:group`, `user:`, and `:group`.","locale":"en"},"2749":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-90","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"The current implementation uses `mount` for three related workflows:","locale":"en"},"2750":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-91","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount`: list all mount points","locale":"en"},"2751":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-92","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount --check`: list mount points and validate UFS reachability","locale":"en"},"2752":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-93","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount <UFS_PATH> <CV_PATH> [OPTIONS]`: create or update a mount","locale":"en"},"2753":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-94","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount resync <CV_PATH> [OPTIONS]`: run metadata resync for an `fs_mode` mount","locale":"en"},"2754":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-95","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"Common options:","locale":"en"},"2755":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations