/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"| Metric Name        | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| operation_duration | Operation duration (classified by type, excluding heartbeats) |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2900":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"The master evaluates every worker heartbeat and client handshake against its\ncompatibility contract and exposes the results as metrics (see\nVersion Management and Compatibility):","locale":"en"},"2901":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name           | Type  | Labels                 | Description                                            |\n| --------------------- | ----- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| compat_worker_verdict | Gauge | `worker_id`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each worker |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2902":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name           | Type  | Labels                   | Description                                            |\n| --------------------- | ----- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| compat_client_verdict | Gauge | `client_addr`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each client |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2903":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name                   | Type    | Labels                 | Description                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| compat_enforce_rejected_total | Counter | `component`, `verdict` | Total number of enforce-mode compatibility rejections |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2904":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"The `verdict` label takes one of: `compatible`, `missing_info`, `blocked`,\n`protocol_mismatch`, `version_too_old`, `version_unknown`. Alert on\n`compat_worker_verdict` / `compat_client_verdict` with a non-`compatible`\nverdict to surface mixed-version clusters, and on `compat_enforce_rejected_total`\nincreases to catch upgrade conflicts early.","locale":"en"},"2905":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-35","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#journal-node-metrics","content":"| Metric Name       | Description          |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- |\n| journal_queue_len | Journal queue length |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2906":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-36","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#journal-node-metrics","content":"| Metric Name         | Description         |\n| ------------------- | 